Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Subject: [PATCH] rcu: Don't dirty rcu_data of CPUs that stayed quiescent

Each grace period's first FQS scan stores a fresh watching snapshot into
the rcu_data of every CPU still holding it up.  For CPUs that stayed
idle or in nohz_full userspace since the previous scan the value is the
same, but the store still pulls their cacheline over, every grace period,
for each of them.

Only store the snapshot when it changed.
---
--- a/kernel/rcu/tree.c
+++ b/kernel/rcu/tree.c
@@ -817,6 +817,8 @@ static void rcu_gpnum_ovf(struct rcu_node *rnp, struct rcu_data *rdp)
  */
 static int rcu_watching_snap_save(struct rcu_data *rdp)
 {
+	int snap;
+
 	/*
 	 * Full ordering between remote CPU's post idle accesses and updater's
 	 * accesses prior to current GP (and also the started GP sequence number)
@@ -828,7 +830,9 @@ static int rcu_watching_snap_save(struct rcu_data *rdp)
 	 * Ordering between remote CPU's pre idle accesses and post grace period
 	 * updater's accesses is enforced by the below acquire semantic.
 	 */
-	rdp->watching_snap = ct_rcu_watching_cpu_acquire(rdp->cpu);
+	snap = ct_rcu_watching_cpu_acquire(rdp->cpu);
+	if (rdp->watching_snap != snap)
+		rdp->watching_snap = snap;
 	if (rcu_watching_snap_in_eqs(rdp->watching_snap)) {
 		trace_rcu_fqs(rcu_state.name, rdp->gp_seq, rdp->cpu, TPS("dti"));
 		rcu_gpnum_ovf(rdp->mynode, rdp);
